  "body": "Source: the Opus second review of PR #2638 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2638#issuecomment-6994872959). PR #2638 fixed #2596.\n\n**Behaviour now**\n\nA loop that has a modelled chamfer on one side only counts as a bevelled loop (`gap`, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs` near L111-118). The generator then chamfers the sharp sides of that loop too. Verify finds the cut on the sharp sides and blocks the post. The result is safe, but the user gets a refusal and no toolpath.\n\n**Wanted**\n\nThe generator judges each side (edge span) of a loop. It chamfers only the spans that the model bevels.\n\n**Done means**\n\n- A test with a loop that has a bevel on one side: the toolpath rides that side only, and verify is clean.\n- The tests of #2596 stay green.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- The work changes a toolpath: safety floor, `effort:high`.\n- Related: #2634, #2635.\n",
